  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 62,
    "summary": "David praises God as his defense, his rock, and his salvation—The Lord judges men according to their works.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him cometh my salvation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He only is my rock and my salvation; he is my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Salvation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "How long will ye imagine mischief against a man? ye shall be slain all of you: as a bowing wall shall ye be, and as a tottering fence.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 115
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They only consult to cast him down from his excellency: they delight in lies: they bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 121,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation is from him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He only is my rock and my salvation: he is my defence; I shall not be moved.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Rock."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In God is my salvation and my glory: the rock of my strength, and my refuge, is in God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Glory."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Refuge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Trust in him at all times; ye people, pour out your heart before him: God is a refuge for us. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely men of low degree are vanity, and men of high degree are a lie: to be laid in the balance, they are altogether lighter than vanity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 137,
            "text": "TG Vanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          },
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 125
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Trust not in oppression, and become not vain in robbery: if riches increase, set not your heart upon them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "OR extortion."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Job 31:25; Luke 12:15; Alma 5:53 (53–56); Hel. 12:2 (1–5); D&C 56:16 (16–18)."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "Jacob 2:19 (18–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "God hath spoken once; twice have I heard this; that power belongeth unto God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Also unto thee, O Lord, belongeth mercy: for thou renderest to every man according to his work.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "Ps. 86:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Good Works; Justice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
